lignment.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Wyoming is the most Republican state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly 23 points toward the GOP. No candidate filings, state polls, or expert ratings exist yet for the 2028 open-seat race, so the outlook rests on fundamentals. National headlines show a climate drifting toward Democrats, with voter discontent and Trump's standing underwater across most states, but Wyoming remains one of the few states where he stays above water.\n\nEven in strong Democratic national years, Wyoming has stayed far out of reach, giving recent Republican nominees some of their largest margins anywhere in the country. With no incumbent on the ballot and no local polling to weigh, the forecast sits close to the state's structural lean, eased by a point or two for the national environment. The Republican nominee is the heavy favorite; the open question is the size of the margin, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.01, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0232, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0282, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.025, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0274, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0226, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0279, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0235, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0258, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0202, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0256, "margin": -23.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0264, "margin": -22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0267